===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{1|rough}}; [[jumpy]]; causing or characterized by [[jolt]]s and [[irregular]] [[movement]]s.
#: {{co|en|a '''bumpy''' ride}}
#: {{co|en|a '''bumpy''' flight}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robin Wasserman|title=Seven Deadly Sins| volume=1: Lust; Envy| year=2013| publisher=Simon and Schuster| page=120| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=LT_O9TOiXPUC&pg=PA120&dq=%22no-tell+motel%22&hl=&cd=18&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22no-tell%20motel%22&f=false| isbn=978-1-4424-7504-5| passage=There was no reason to pull off the interstate and drive twenty miles down a '''bumpy''' local road, just to stay in a dilapidated no-tell motel.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Elisabeth Malkin and Ana Swanson|title=Mexico Ratifies Trade Deal With the U.S. and Canada|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/06/19/world/americas/mexico-nafta-usa-canada.html|date=2019-06-19|passage=The path to approval has been '''bumpiest''' in Washington, where Democrats in Congress have raised concerns over Mexico’s enforcement of labor rights and environmental law — and smoothest in Mexico, where the president has described the accord as a guarantee of stability for his country’s economy.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Julie Weed|title=Sick of Bumpy, Delayed Flights? New Weather Tech Could Help.|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/05/travel/ai-technology-flights-weather.html|date=2023-05-05|passage=So, will flights just get '''bumpier''' and delays even more common? Not necessarily.}}
# Covered with or full of [[bump]]s.
#: {{cot|en|lumpy}}
#: {{co|en|'''bumpy''' road}}

